# .graphifyignore — Brain repo
#
# Narrows Graphify's scan to Brain-relevant source files only.
# Graphify reads this file (prefers it over .gitignore) per gitignore spec.
# The .gitignore covers runtime/generated exclusions for git; this file
# explicitly scopes the graph to code/docs worth indexing semantically.
#
# Why a separate .graphifyignore?
# Brain contains embedded third-party codebases (firecrawl: 1171 files,
# model-selector venv, codex computer-use apps) and large data files that
# cause Graphify semantic chunk overflow even after git-tracked filters.
# The brain-runtime profile `exclude` list is declarative metadata only
# (not passed to Graphify CLI). This file is Graphify's actual scan scope.
#
# Rule: exclude anything that is not Brain-authored infrastructure,
# skills, specs, runbooks, or tools.

# ── VCS & OS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# ── Build / compiled artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
build/
.next/
**/.next/
coverage/
node-compile-cache/
**/node-compile-cache/

# ── Python environments & caches ──────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
**/.venv/
**/.venv*/
**/venv/
**/env/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# ── Graphify output (canonical output path, never input) ──────────────────
graphify-out/
.graphify-out/

# ── Brain runtime scratch ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
runtime/local/
projects/runtime/
.ai/
